# Sample 20 — Secondary axis
#
# `secondary axis` adds a second calibrated axis on the other side of
# the plot, relabelling the SAME physical positions in a different
# quantity — here, MVA at the diagram's nominal voltage — rather than
# plotting anything new. Useful when the audience for a report thinks
# in MVA but the underlying protection settings are all current-based.

diagram "Feeder setting — MVA cross-reference" {
  voltage 33 kV
  show current, mva
  secondary axis top MVA

  below "Maximum load" must 3.5 kA
  below "Emergency load" must 5 kA margin 10%
  above "Minimum 2-phase fault" must 8 kA margin 10%
  above "Minimum 3-phase fault" must 12 kA margin 10%

  selected "Selected setting" midpoint step 0.05 kA
}
